{
 "about": "Shared media and timestamp vectors (spec amendments C1-C4); generated by tests/python/make_media_vectors.py, do not edit. `input` is the cell text, or {parts: [[text, count], ...]} meaning the concatenation of each text repeated count times. Accepted vectors carry the facts both sides must report: base64 -> decoded length and sha256; image -> format, width, height; audio -> sampleRate, channels, frames; timestamp -> epochMs (UTC; a fractional part carries microseconds, compare within 0.002 ms). Header walks visit at most maxChunks chunks or segments (PNG: IHDR to IEND inclusive; JPEG: markers after SOI up to and including SOS; WAV: chunks after the RIFF header).",
